  "notes": "The research is explicit that the solo records are \"a measurably different parameter set from the duo\", and the measurable difference is tempo: 76–89 centred on **80**, a full ~10 BPM below the Clipse spine and one of the tightest clusters in the section. That single number is the main reason this is not a mode of `clipse`. The second is key: \"C minor dominates the 2018–2022 records (five separate readings)\", so `session.keys` is weighted 6:2:2 toward Cm rather than the archetype's even spread. Everything else is subtraction of a different kind from the duo's — where Clipse builds a woodblock figure at −3 dB, this is \"sample-loop rap, not programmed trap… several records run the loop with almost no kit\", so `percs` drops to 0–1 hits at −11 dB and the hats sit non-continuous at the 0.28 floor. \"No replayed chords… the loop *is* the melodic content\" is `impliedByRiff` with `chordDurationBeats` 2–24. `arrangement.structures` drops the bridge entirely and both forms end on a hook-tag, because the research says \"seven-track albums, no sung choruses, no bridge — verse / hook-tag / verse, cold starts, hard stops\". ⚠ Where 808s appear they sit under a 2&4 backbeat rather than a half-time one, which the research says is what keeps this model out of `trap`; `session.halfTime` stays false for that reason. ⚠ Producers **Kanye West**, **Just Blaze** and **Swizz Beatz** have their own entries and are cited, not restated. ⚠ `confidence` is medium (research: high-medium) and the tempo/key bands are marked `[LOW-CONF]` — algorithmic readings, with 150–164 folding in half onto 75–82. The `i–VII` and `i–iv` families at weights 2 and 1 are **INFERRED**; the research names static `i` only. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 44 to 38 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 39 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 6.",
